usb: typec: ucsi: Drop an empty object ahead of the PDOs

On the Dell XPS 14 DA14260, the PPM answers GET_PDOS for the partner's
source capabilities with an empty object first. A 100 W charger offering
5, 9, 12, 15 and 20 V and a PPS range comes back as 0, 5 V, 9 V, 12 V at
offset 0 and 15 V, 20 V, PPS at offset 4. The RDO names object position
5, the 20 V PDO, but src_pdos[4] holds 15 V, so voltage_now reads 15 V
on a 20 V contract. The partner's capabilities stop at the first empty
PDO, so they register with none.

The first PDO is always the vSafe5V Fixed Supply and never empty, so an
empty one there is dropped and the rest move up.

diff -ruN a/drivers/usb/typec/ucsi/ucsi.c b/drivers/usb/typec/ucsi/ucsi.c
--- a/drivers/usb/typec/ucsi/ucsi.c
+++ b/drivers/usb/typec/ucsi/ucsi.c
@@ -899,16 +899,29 @@
 		return ret;
 
 	num_pdos = ret / sizeof(u32); /* number of bytes to 32-bit PDOs */
-	if (num_pdos < UCSI_MAX_PDOS)
-		return num_pdos;
+	if (num_pdos == UCSI_MAX_PDOS) {
+		/* get the remaining PDOs, if any */
+		ret = ucsi_read_pdos(con, role, is_partner, pdos, UCSI_MAX_PDOS,
+				     PDO_MAX_OBJECTS - UCSI_MAX_PDOS);
+		if (ret < 0)
+			return ret;
 
-	/* get the remaining PDOs, if any */
-	ret = ucsi_read_pdos(con, role, is_partner, pdos, UCSI_MAX_PDOS,
-			     PDO_MAX_OBJECTS - UCSI_MAX_PDOS);
-	if (ret < 0)
-		return ret;
+		num_pdos += ret / sizeof(u32);
+	}
+
+	/*
+	 * Some PPMs put an empty object ahead of the PDOs. The first PDO is
+	 * always the vSafe5V Fixed Supply, so an empty one is never real, and
+	 * left in place it puts every PDO one position late: the RDO's object
+	 * position then names the wrong PDO, and the capabilities stop at it.
+	 */
+	if (num_pdos && !pdos[0]) {
+		num_pdos--;
+		memmove(pdos, pdos + 1, num_pdos * sizeof(u32));
+		pdos[num_pdos] = 0;
+	}
 
-	return ret / sizeof(u32) + num_pdos;
+	return num_pdos;
 }
 
 static int ucsi_get_src_pdos(struct ucsi_connector *con)
